 "business_summary": "Space Exploration Technologies Corp. (SPCX) has three segments (SEC 10-Q, Note 1). Space makes and launches reusable rockets, including Starship R&D. Connectivity runs the Starlink broadband and mobile network. AI covers Grok, the X platform, AI solutions and AI compute infrastructure; xAI/X were folded in via the common-control xAI Merger on 2026-02-02. The company IPO'd in June 2026, selling 638.9M Class A shares at $135.00 for net proceeds of $85,675M, and issued $25,000M of SpaceX Notes (SEC 10-Q, Notes 1 and 9). Q2 2026 revenue was $7,814M versus $4,071M a year earlier, up 91.9%. Connectivity contributed $4,291M and AI $2,561M, of which AI infrastructure grew by about $1,600M from new cloud-services contracts. Space contributed $962M (SEC 10-Q, Note 3 and MD&A). Consolidated GAAP operating loss was $(143)M in Q2 and $(2,086)M in H1. Capex is very heavy at $28,476M in H1 2026, mostly AI data centers, so free cash flow is deeply negative (SEC 10-Q, cash flow statement; MARKET DATA history). The stock trades at $167.38 with a market cap of about $2.2T (MARKET DATA).",
