 "recommended_base_growth_rate": null,
 "growth_rationale": "No defensible annual FCF growth rate can be set. FCF is negative and worsening: $(5,387)M in 2024, $(14,121)M in 2025 (MARKET DATA) and about $(25,010)M in H1 2026 alone (computed from the SEC 10-Q). Percentage growth off a negative base is not meaningful, and capex is rising faster than operating cash flow (H1 2026 capex $28,476M vs OCF $3,466M). Revenue growth is strong, but it is partly one-time-step: Q2 AI revenue includes ~$1,600M of new AI infrastructure cloud revenue, and those contracts can be terminated on 90 days' notice after the ramp period (SEC 10-Q, Item 1A). Sell-side consensus implies revenue of $44.68B in 2026 and $113.5B in 2027 (+154%) with 2027 EPS of $1.94 (Yahoo Finance - Analysis). That is a revenue/EPS forecast, not an FCF forecast, and it has a very wide range (revenue $59.42B-$189.46B). Management gives no FCF or capex guidance in the provided documents, and it says it can reduce or reallocate data-center capex (SEC 10-Q, Liquidity). A DCF would need an explicit capex normalization and margin path, which the material does not provide, so the answer is null rather than a guess.",
