 "why_questionable": "It implies H2 2026 revenue of about $32B against H1 of $12.5B, which is a doubling per quarter. It has a wide range ($59B to $189B), and it is a revenue and EPS view with no FCF or capex input. A $2.2T cap capitalizes 2027 EPS at 86x, even assuming the targets are met. Analyst estimates after a hot IPO tend to be biased upward."
 },
 {
