st a $167.38 market price, a gap of about $32B in market terms. The filings analysis flags this, but the qualitative section ignores it. The accounting measurement at close (fair value versus fixed price) is unexplained.","The 'sources of cash' comfort ($100B) ignores that debt and related-party leaseback financing are rising as the company also raised equity. The financial summary mentions the technical default but the qualitative section describes capital access as a moat.","Typographical and tie-out issues: SBC is $1,570M in equity versus $1,580M in the cash flow statement plus capitalized amounts, and debt prepayment penalties total $1,164M against $1,153M paid. These are small but add to the picture of weak controls at a new filer."],"severity":"major","severity_reason":"The core thesis depends on an AI build-out (1.4GW to about 10GW by end-2027) that the stated capex pace and the $100B cash balance cannot fund without large new debt or equity. FCF is about -$25B in H1 alone and the burn is accelerating. The recent revenue acceleration rests on concentrated, 90-day-cancellable AI cloud contracts, with possible circularity through the Cursor deal. Unit economics are unproven, with the AI segment at a $(3.7)B H1 operating loss. The 10-Q has internal contradictions on debt, a covenant default occurred, and billions sit in related-party failed sale-leaseback debt. Governance gives public shareholders essentially no recourse. At about 96x sales and 17x book, this is a reason to avoid or underweight regardless of valuation, until funding, AI margins and customer concentration are shown to be sound."}

